(20-LAZY-DINNERS-SORTED-BY-HOW-TIRED-YOU-ARE.HTML) Tj
T*
(WHAT'S FOR EATS  |  PRINTABLE DINNER GUIDE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(22 Cozy Fall Dinners That Taste Like Wearing Your Favorite Sweater) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Easy fall dinner ideas with real, step-by-step recipes, sorted by the tool you feel like) Tj
T*
(using tonight.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(There's a moment in October when your kitchen stops smelling like summer and starts) Tj
T*
(smelling like decisions. The windows stay shut. The oven stops being an appliance and) Tj
T*
(becomes a personality trait. And somewhere around 5:15 p.m., you realize you want dinner) Tj
T*
(to do what a good sweater does: wrap around you, run a little too warm, and make you say) Tj
T*
("I'm not leaving" before you've even sat down.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(That's the whole idea here. Fall food isn't about being fancy. It's soft, savory, a) Tj
T*
(little sweet and forgiving. A sweater doesn't care if you're wearing it wrong, and) Tj
T*
(neither do these recipes. If you've never cooked anything more ambitious than toast,) Tj
T*
(you're in the right place. Every recipe below tells you what to buy, what to do in what) Tj
T*
(order, and what it should look, smell and sound like at each stage, so you're never) Tj
T*
(guessing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(I sorted all 22 by cooking method: soups, casseroles, slow cooker and sheet pan.) Tj
T*
(Dreading the chopping? Head to the slow cooker. Only want one pan to wash? Sheet pan) Tj
T*
(section, right this way. Each recipe lists time and cost. Cost key \(rough estimate for a) Tj
T*
(family of four; prices vary by store\): $ = under about $12, $$ = about $12 to $20.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Before you start: a five-line beginner cheat sheet) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Simmer) Tj
T*
(= small, lazy bubbles breaking the surface now and then. A full rolling boil is the soup) Tj
T*
(equivalent of a toddler tantrum.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Saut) Tj
T*
(= cook in a bit of fat over medium heat, stirring so nothing burns. You'll hear a gentle) Tj
T*
(sizzle. Loud crackling means turn the heat down.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fork-tender) Tj
T*
(= a fork slides into the food with no resistance, like a spoon into soft butter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rest) Tj
T*
(= leave the food alone for a few minutes after cooking so juices settle and you don't) Tj
T*
(burn your mouth. It's mandatory, not optional.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Thermometer?) Tj
T*
(A cheap instant-read one is the best $12 a beginner cook can spend. Chicken and turkey) Tj
T*
(are safe at 165 F, pork chops at 145 F plus a 3-minute rest, ground beef at 160 F.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Quick plan:) Tj
T*
(pick one dinner from each section for the week. After the recipes you'll find three) Tj
T*
(cheap tricks that make everything taste like you tried harder, plus a free Fall Dinner) Tj
T*
(Bingo card.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Soups That Count as a Hug) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
