T*
() Tj
T*
(How to make it) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Melt 2 tbsp butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onion and cook 5 to 6) Tj
T*
(minutes, stirring now and then, until soft and see-through \(translucent\), not browned.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Stir in the garlic and cook just 30 seconds. You'll smell it right away. Garlic burns) Tj
T*
(fast, so move on as soon as the kitchen smells amazing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Pour in the tomatoes with all their juice, the broth, sugar, salt and pepper. Use your) Tj
T*
(spoon to squish the tomatoes against the side of the pot.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Bring to a gentle simmer, then lower the heat and cook, partly covered, for 15 minutes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Blend until smooth. An immersion \(stick\) blender is easiest: dip it straight in the pot.) Tj
T*
(With a regular blender, work in batches, fill it no more than halfway, and hold a folded) Tj
T*
(towel over the lid. Hot soup builds steam pressure and can pop the lid off.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Return the soup to the pot over low heat and stir in the cream. Taste and add salt if it) Tj
T*
(needs it. Keep it warm while you make the croutons.) Tj
T*
